            "title": "Have You Played Fishy?",
            "date": "2019-08-29 02:30:46",
            "url": "https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/rps/2415540140455497758",
            "notes": "<p><a href=\"https://assets.rockpapershotgun.com/images/2019/07/Fishyheader.jpg\"><img src=\"https://assets.rockpapershotgun.com/images/2019/07/Fishyheader.jpg/RPSS/resize/690x-1/format/jpg//RPSS/resize/670x-1/format/jpg/\" width=\"670\" /></a></p>\n<aside><em><a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/tag/have-you-played/\">Have You Played?</a> is an endless stream of game retrospectives. One a day, every day, perhaps for all time.</em></aside>\n<p>It   s strange to go back to a game you vividly remember playing when you were ten. Sat in front of your primary school   s computers, cannily placed to give visitors the impression we were modern and hip. Whiling away a lonely lunchtime, eating progressively bigger fish in <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/game/fishy/\">Fishy</a>.</p>\n<p> <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/2019/08/29/have-you-played-fishy/#more-709303\" class=\"more-link\"><span aria-label=\"Continue reading Have You Played&#8230; Fishy?\">(more&hellip;)</span></a></p>\n"
        }
